  "body": "What happens (v0.26.0, macOS): every cloud provider fails on Send with \"no Anthropic API key: set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or store one in the OS keychain\" (same for OpenAI, Gemini). The app has no field for the key. An environment variable needs a relaunch, and an app started from the Dock does not see shell variables. The keychain needs a Terminal command (`security add-generic-password -s camcraft-ai -a anthropic -w`). The user also learns that the key is missing only after a message fails.\n\nExpected:\n1. \"Set API key...\" per cloud provider in the AI Chat panel. It stores the key in the OS keychain under the names the app already reads (`KEYCHAIN_SERVICE` = camcraft-ai, accounts anthropic/openai/gemini; `crates/app/src/ai/secret.rs`, `keychain.rs`). It never shows the key again. Remove and Test buttons. The key is never written to the project file or logs.\n2. A status line as soon as a provider is chosen: \"Ready (key from keychain / environment)\", \"No key - Set API key...\", \"Ollama not running at <url>\", \"model <m> not installed\".\n3. Links beside the key field, opened in the browser: where to get or top up a key (Anthropic console billing, OpenAI platform billing, Google AI Studio keys, Ollama download).\n\nWorkaround: the `security` command above, or set the variable and start the app from a shell.\n\nDone means: a new user sets a key, sees \"Ready\" and gets an answer without leaving the app. UI structural tests pin the button, the status states and that the key text is never drawn after save.\n\nUser validation (reporter, 2026-11-23): before this merges, the reporter (mkinney) hand-tests a build of the PR in the desktop app and confirms it is usable. The PR stays a draft until that confirmation is on the PR.\n",
